<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:12Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt: Digesting the AfD's landmark election win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:016746796c2f191e1cab4af558fdbc454e3666762dc2370a7cee94cec789bbc4</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T21:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-digesting-the-afd-s-landmark-election-win/a-79103981--03f4036eaf84.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-digesting-the-afd-s-landmark-election-win/a-79103981?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With well over 40% for the far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD), Saxony-Anhalt has witnessed a landmark election night. DW's reporters were on the ground.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>AfD wants to form a government in Saxony-Anhalt — but how?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e6e13a2fae22a75cccd2a3151c051860c74262f3c1df9aa487bda91bff24bcf</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T21:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afd-wants-to-form-a-government-in-saxony-anhalt-but-how/a-79107331--c787b4b85cbe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afd-wants-to-form-a-government-in-saxony-anhalt-but-how/a-79107331?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following its record-breaking success in the state election, the far-right AfD in Saxony-Anhalt is aiming to form a government.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany plans anti-drone shield over Leipzig attack — report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:21b036ca2d3c780bd3e924f5e2ab67aa2dff44955325c5d8b91d3b5b7fed9016</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T10:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-plans-anti-drone-shield-over-leipzig-attack-report/a-79052604--572615382eed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-plans-anti-drone-shield-over-leipzig-attack-report/a-79052604?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Several German cities will receive rapidly deployable units capable of defending against drone strikes on critical infrastructure, according to Bild am Sonntag newspaper.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German company successfully launches rocket to space</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:576212affbf541f2bf1105c23b4e3ed8716acd611be3ee463099f6f533e8c9e6</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T22:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-company-successfully-launches-rocket-to-space/a-79050717--59c961471bc2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-company-successfully-launches-rocket-to-space/a-79050717?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bavaria-based Isar Aerospace managed to launch its Spectrum rocket into orbit, 18 months after its first attempt. This is the first such launch from European soil.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Croatia: Toxic waste protest draws tens of thousands</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd60035923213e097ad9864d8cda40e076a0038d18d5f2e2cdaf9e47ede9dcb9</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T17:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/croatia-toxic-waste-protest-draws-tens-of-thousands/a-79049228--9dec1bdce80c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/croatia-toxic-waste-protest-draws-tens-of-thousands/a-79049228?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Zagreb demonstrators demanded that the government come up with a plan to clear illegal toxic waste in 20 days. Prime Minister Plenkovic has promised to tackle the issue.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Thousands march at Saxony-Anhalt rallies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a14d4dca78bb2d6e23c224b32a44bea0e8ccfc7787b9af36c9b5f381bd37581</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T06:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-thousands-march-at-saxony-anhalt-rallies/live-79041302--28cda5652dc8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-thousands-march-at-saxony-anhalt-rallies/live-79041302?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ahead of Saxony-Anhalt's state election on Sunday, a democracy festival by civil society groups has been held in Magdeburg. The far-right AfD organized its final campaign rally in the state capital.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Election fraud claims spread in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8dedf9f5f054dad5e97d07e7aa8c328080249dc6f6cd846b8470f12a84641fcf</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T19:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-election-fraud-claims-spread-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79093254--984abe33c1c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-election-fraud-claims-spread-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79093254?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">False and misleading claims are raising questions about the integrity of the election in Saxony-Anhalt. DW Fact Check takes a closer look.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt's state election will have a nationwide impact</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:84807bef320bc5be5b0e6e7c4529a9cb4fa94b93a63a2955d5ad657805267e72</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T18:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-s-state-election-will-have-a-nationwide-impact/a-78874569--8cf3f82cd3a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-s-state-election-will-have-a-nationwide-impact/a-78874569?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The election in the eastern state of Saxony-Anhalt could have dramatic consequences for Germany's federal government. Pollsters point to dissatisfaction with Chancellor Merz as one reason for his party's poor showing.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Germany's postal voting system isn't rigged</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d722a670c3dfa99ddee3eb5f2a6289ca9a2ecdc7c7cc6913fde56cc644dcf224</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T18:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-germany-s-postal-voting-system-isn-t-rigged/a-78958438--ffb06136be22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-germany-s-postal-voting-system-isn-t-rigged/a-78958438?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ahead of Germany's state elections in September, rumors began circulating on social media claiming that postal voting is not secure — claims that have also been made about other elections. Here's why they're wrong.</summary><category term="German election" /></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt election: Why the AfD is so strong</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:22e0747610b3d78713a8b2bc980fa107cbb60589b477b507ef7337c12ad50f31</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T18:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-election-why-the-afd-is-so-strong/a-78482588--f7f12ed5af71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-election-why-the-afd-is-so-strong/a-78482588?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The AfD has emerged as the strongest party in Germany's eastern state of Saxony-Anhalt by a wide margin. What is driving support for the far right in this predominantly rural eastern German state?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany, Kosovo unite against ticks carrying deadly virus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:97d595e88864fa0fe1e9b530996793423679d879bc4a76729e537d2382263330</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T10:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-kosovo-unite-against-ticks-carrying-deadly-virus/a-78655223--2c267f5d11c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-kosovo-unite-against-ticks-carrying-deadly-virus/a-78655223?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has high-security labs while Kosovo has Hyalomma ticks and experience with the deadly Crimean-Congo hemorrhagic fever. Working together, German and Kosovar scientists are fighting the disease and its vectors.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>2026 Beethoven Festival evokes a sense of home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c777745376a259b01095507fe728c3ed333df3f05fffb31ca46cc771cafe938</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T08:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/2026-beethoven-festival-evokes-a-sense-of-home/a-78892997--9bbbc99c220c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/2026-beethoven-festival-evokes-a-sense-of-home/a-78892997?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The motto of this year's classical music festival in Bonn is "Home/At Home," featuring musicians from diverse cultures presenting pieces from their homelands.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>This extremely successful author polarizes German readers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4765e6e6fad7586d29435c2658a2374d09b1ecddc0a542b7f9c814c2fb9465ab</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T07:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452--1ca180b39c00.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">She's young and she says what she thinks: Caroline Wahl is topping Germany's bestseller lists with her novels. But she has also faced a public backlash.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's military wants to recruit tech-savvy gamers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92c2db82dae4a4580ce0ad6671f3326ef7b9f59bff909dbcfa0c52487272de87</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T10:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-military-wants-to-recruit-tech-savvy-gamers/a-78536462--a4ab0409cda1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-military-wants-to-recruit-tech-savvy-gamers/a-78536462?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Bundeswehr has been a fixture at Gamescom, Cologne's video game trade fair, for years. But critics say military recruitment does not belong at an entertainment convention.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
